  "description": "QOVBAI crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P 21 21 2. Reported CIF formula moiety: H3 O1 1+,C120 H176 Dy9 N24 O42 1-,3(C2 H3 N1),8(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy9 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.551-5.047 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 88.83-166.31°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula (H3O)[Dy9(HL1)8(μ4-O)2(μ3-OH)8(OAc)8]·3CH3CN·8CH3OH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
